        "item_KYMPUf": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What's the difference between Shabbat candles and memorial candles?",
            "text": "<p>Shabbat candles are lit to welcome the Sabbath and typically burn for about 4 hours on Friday evenings. Memorial candles,  including Yahrzeit and Yizkor candles, are intended to burn much longer, often through a full 24-hour period, as a way of honoring the memory of someone who has passed. The two serve distinct purposes and are generally not interchangeable.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
